No, you have.
不，你就是。

163
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:36.440
I think you know that you are good at loving people and being loved.
我觉得你知道自己很擅长去爱别人以及被人爱。

164
00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.580
I like helping people.
我喜欢帮助别人。

165
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:38.960
I do.
我是真的喜欢。

166
00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:39.500
Yeah.
对。

167
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.520
So maybe there is something there that I like to be of service and needed.
所以也许其中有些东西，让我喜欢去效劳和被需要。

168
00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.240
My second highest score, though, was the challenger.
不过，我第二高的得分是挑战型。

169
00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.700
Oh, same as Amy Poehler.
噢，和艾米·波勒一样。

170
00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.360
I charge into a room.
我冲进一个房间。

171
00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.080
Yeah.
对。

172
00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.980
And want to help you aggressively.
然后想要极其热情地帮你。

173
00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.000
You know what's interesting?
你知道有趣的是什么吗？

174
00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.400
My helper score is very low.
我的助人型得分很低。

175
00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.380
The helper.
助人型。

176
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.280
52% the helper.
52%是助人型。

177
00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.220
My second was the achiever.
我的第二高是成就型。

178
00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.600
So I'm a reformer and an achiever, I guess.
所以我想我是一个改革者和一个成就者。

179
00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.040
Well, my the reformer score is 80%.
好吧，我的改革者得分是80%。

180
00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.500
Oh, you're there.
噢，你跟我一样。

181
00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.760
You're with me.
你跟我是一伙的。

182
00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.480
What's your lowest score?
你最低的分数是多少？

183
00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.860
My lowest was the peacemaker.
我最低的是和平型。

184
00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.980
I don't know what that means.
我不知道这代表什么。

185
00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.100
My peacemaker is right in the middle.
我的和平型得分正好在中游。

186
00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:22.660
It's 83.
是83。

187
00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.840
My lowest was, this makes me sound like such a basic bitch.
我最低的是，这让我听起来真像个烂大街的普通碧池。

188
00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.520
My lowest score was the individualiSt.
我最低的分数是个性型。

189
00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.670
I just want to go with the flow.
我只是想随波逐流。

190
00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:42.350
You know, I remember the questions that I think might have like pertained to being a person
你知道的，我还记得那些我认为可能跟扮演这种角色有关的问题

191
00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.370
who is the peacemaker.
也就是和平制造者。

192
00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:48.490
You know, because it's all like strongly agree, agree, neutral, disagree, strongly disagree.
你知道，因为全都是强力赞同、赞同、中立、反对、强力反对这种选项。

193
00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:53.490
And I feel like peacemaker questions were things like, it's very hard for me when people are in
我觉得和平型的问题大概是这种：当人们处于

194
00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:53.890
conflict.
冲突中时，对我来说很难受。

195
00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:54.830
It's not hard for me.
对我来说并不难受。

196
00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.230
I don't feel the need to make peace.
我觉得没有必要去维持和平。

197
00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:04.310
I think we can spend time in a messy, confrontational space where we're figuring things out.
我觉得我们可以花时间在一个混乱、对抗的空间里，在那里把事情理清楚。

198
00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.370
It's okay.
没关系的。

199
00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.310
Yeah, I don't know.
嗯，我不知道。

200
00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.670
I have to say, I was not a fan of the teSt.
我得说，我不太喜欢这个测试。

201
00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.630
I don't like tests that are like multiple choice.
我不喜欢那种多选题的测试。

202
00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.870
How would you have done the test differently?
换作你的话，你会怎么设计这个测试？

203
00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:16.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

204
00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.170
This is not my job to create the teSt.
出题可不是我的工作。

205
00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.410
But I'm just saying I wasn't a fan.
但我只是说我不太喜欢。

206
00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:28.750
I don't like strongly agree, agree, neutral, disagree, strongly disagree.
我不喜欢“非常同意、同意、中立、不同意、非常不同意”这种选项。

207
00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.390
Did you strongly agree or strongly disagree to things?
对于那些问题，你选的是非常同意还是非常不同意？

208
00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:33.050
Sometimes.
有时会。

209
00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.010
Yeah, same.
对，我也是。

210
00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:34.450
Same.
一样。

211
00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.410
I strongly agreed to a lot of stuff.
我有很多项都选了非常同意。

212
00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.330
Well, you're a reformer.
嗯，你是个改良主义者。

213
00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:39.770
Yeah.
对。

214
00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.390
It's true, I guess.
也是，我想是的。

215
00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.970
Well, it was very interesting.
嗯，这非常有趣。

216
00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.490
Sam, have you taken this test?
萨姆，你做过这个测试吗？

217
00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.410
No, I haven't.
没有，我没做过。

218
00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:48.290
I'm going to take it right now.
我这就去做。

219
00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.950
Oh, will you tell us at the end what your score is?
哦，你最后能告诉我们你的得分是多少吗？

220
00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:51.630
Okay.
好的。

221
00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.670
Do you want us to send it to you, the one that we took?
你想让我们把我们做的那份发给你吗？

222
00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:54.270
Yes, I would.
好啊。

223
00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.350
It costs $1.50 to get your results.
获取测试结果要花1.50美元。

224
00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:57.410
I'm more than willing to pay.
我非常乐意付钱。

225
00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.390
I'm pretty sure now I'm going to be on an email list too.
我挺确信现在我也要被加入某个邮件列表了。

226
00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:01.130
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

227
00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:02.490
Your information's sold for sure.
你的信息肯定被卖了。

228
00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:02.970
Yeah.
对。

229
00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.050
Well, Carolyn, there you go.
好吧，卡罗琳，这不就来了嘛。

230
00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.290
If I ever go on good hang, I'll know my score.
如果我以后去上什么好玩的节目，我就会知道我的得分了。

231
00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.590
That's good, right?
那挺好的，对吧？

232
00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:11.410
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

233
00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.190
And I want to ask her about being the challenger.
我想问问她关于成为挑战者的事。

234
00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.930
Yeah, you share that.
对，你们俩有同感。

235
00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:16.990
I do.
是的。

236
00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.550
That's number two on my liSt.
那在我单子上排第二。

237
00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:18.910
I know.
我知道。

238
00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:20.290
All right.
好吧。

239
00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.390
Well, everyone, why don't we take a break?
各位，我们休息一下怎么样？

240
00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:26.130
And when we come back, buckle in, because it's Michael Scott Candy Bag.
等我们回来后，都系好安全带，因为接下来是迈克尔·斯科特的糖果袋环节。

241
00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.670
And to kick things off, I thought we needed a little candy.
为了拉开序幕，我想我们需要一点糖果。

242
00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:42.770
Like real life candy?
现实生活中的糖果吗？

243
00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:43.730
Real candy.
真正的糖果。

244
00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.730
What did you bring?
你带了什么？

245
00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:49.290
Well, I wanted to know, did Michael Scott have a favorite candy?
嗯，我想知道，迈克尔·斯科特有什么最喜欢的糖果吗？

246
00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.950
Is it like the whatchamacallit or something?
是像“大眼鸡”巧克力棒那类东西吗？

247
00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.050
Well, that's not his favorite.
嗯，那个不是他最喜欢的。

248
00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.590
And I couldn't find anything really specifically.
而且我也没查到什么具体的信息。

249
00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.590
He loves sweets.
他喜欢吃甜食。

250
00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.470
We know that.
我们都知道这一点。

251
00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:04.830
But in the meeting, season six, episode two, he does try to share his love of jelly beans
但在第六季第二集的会议中，他确实尝试与吉姆

252
00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.350
with Jim.
分享他对果冻豆的喜爱。

253
00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.430
So I brought jelly beans.
所以我带了果冻豆。

254
00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:07.390
Oh, great.
哦，太好了。

255
00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.030
There you go.
给你。

256
00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:11.770
And have some jelly beans.
吃点果冻豆吧。

257
00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:12.250
Okay.
好的。

258
00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:13.550
Do you like jelly beans?
你喜欢果冻豆吗？

259
00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:14.790
I do.
我喜欢。

260
00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:15.890
What's not to like?
有什么理由不喜欢呢？

261
00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:16.570
I know.
我也觉得。

262
00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.150
I like them too.
我也喜欢。

263
00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:18.570
I love jelly beans.
我超爱果冻豆。

264
00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:20.030
I even love some funky flavors.
我甚至喜欢一些奇奇怪怪的风味。

265
00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:20.570
Oh.
哦。

266
00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:23.770
So do you like a jelly belly that has like a real flavor?
那你喜欢那种原汁原味的吉利豆吗？

267
00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:25.850
Or do you like the ones that I brought?
还是喜欢我带来的这种？

268
00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:30.530
These are just like your typical like Brock's tiny jelly beans.
这些就像是布洛克斯的典型小果冻豆。

269
00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:31.930
Like the kind you have at Easter.
就像复活节时吃的那种。

270
00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.450
Guess where mine are from?
猜猜我的从哪来的？

271
00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:34.210
Easter.
复活节。

272
00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:34.510
Yeah.
对。

273
00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.270
The outside was a little crunchy.
外皮有点脆脆的。

274
00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.970
Well, I want them out of my house.
总之，我想把它们清出我的屋子。

275
00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:40.410
You were?
你是吗？

276
00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.070
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

277
00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:41.510
It's pre-cleaning.
这算是大扫除前的清理。

278
00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.310
I was like talking to you and you were telling me all the different stuff you were cleaning
我当时在跟你聊天，你跟我讲了你正在清理的

279
00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:45.590
out.
各种东西。

280
00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.770
So I guess you just got rid of your jelly beans.
所以我猜你只是顺便把果冻豆处理掉了。

281
00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.510
Well, I'm lucky Michael Scott liked them.
好吧，我很庆幸迈克尔·斯科特喜欢它们。

282
00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:50.330
So it worked out.
所以结果还挺好。

283
00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:50.690
You are.
你确实很庆幸。

284
00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:55.750
So listen, I was also really curious when we said we were going to dig into these and
所以听着，当我们要深入探讨这些时，我也很好奇，

285
00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:01.490
I wanted to get into the context of like, how did the candy bags work from a production
我想了解一下背景，从制作的角度来看，

286
00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:02.130
standpoint?
糖果袋是如何运作的？

287
00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:10.450
You know, like, how would they decide which version of a scene or a talking head to use?
你知道的，比如，他们是如何决定使用某个场景或独白镜头的哪个版本的？

288
00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:17.470
So we reached out to Dave Rogers to ask him and we said when he would do his assembly,
所以我们联系了戴夫·罗杰斯来问他，我们问当他进行粗剪时，

289
00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:21.870
when he would do his editor's pass, would he use the scripted version or did he have
当他进行剪辑师审片时，他是会用剧本版还是有

290
00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.010
license to put in the candy bag one?
权限放进糖果袋版？

291
00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.110
Like, how are these things organized?
比如，这些东西是怎么组织的？

292
00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.450
How did it all work?
这一切到底是怎么运作的？

293
00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.650
This is very much your producer brain wanting to figure it out, which I love about you.
这完全是你那充满制片人思维的大脑想要搞明白的事，我太喜欢你这一点了。

294
00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.370
Well, here's what Dave said.
好吧，戴夫是这么说的。

295
00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:36.910
By the way, Dave always gets back to us right away.
顺便说一句，戴夫总是第一时间回复我们。

296
00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:37.370
I know.
我知道。

297
00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.270
I know I say it a gazillion times, but I love him.
我知道我已经说过无数次了，但我太爱他了。

298
00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:44.190
He said, we would get all of the takes of a talking head and the assistant editors would
他说，我们会拿到独白的所有镜头，助理剪辑师通常

299
00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:47.970
usually label them as alt A, alt B, et cetera.
会把它们标记为备用A、备用B等等。

300
00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:52.510
And the editors would watch them all and put into the assembly whatever take they liked the
然后剪辑师会看完全部，并把他们喜欢的任何镜头放进

301
00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:52.850
beSt.
最棒的。

302
00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:58.090
It did not matter if it was the scripted line or a must shoot alt or a candy bag alt.
无论是剧本台词、备选镜头还是“糖果袋”备选台词，都无所谓。

303
00:11:58.430 --> 00:11:59.850
Same for scenes in the show.
剧中的场景也是如此。

304
00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:04.170
It didn't matter to the editors if a line was officially scripted or if there was a new joke
对剪辑师来说，不管是正式剧本里的台词，还是编剧在片场临时提的新笑话

305
00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:07.530
or dialogue that a writer pitched on set or an actor improvised.
或是演员即兴发挥的对话，都无所谓。

306
00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:13.370
Once a scene was filmed and ready to edit, whatever was the funniest and best served the show
只要一个场景拍完准备剪辑，只要是最搞笑、最符合节目效果的内容

307
00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.750
and that made it into the cut.
就会被剪进正片里。

308
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.510
But very interesting.
但真的很有趣。

309
00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:23.270
So the editors really had a lot of agency to go through that footage and kind of pick
所以剪辑师确实有很大的自主权去翻看这些素材，并挑选

310
00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:24.690
what they thought worked beSt.
他们认为效果最好的部分。

311
00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:24.990
Yeah.
对。

312
00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:29.430
Remember, Jenna, when you and I co-presented at the Editor's Awards?
还记得吗，珍娜，当我和你一起在剪辑师奖上担任颁奖嘉宾的时候？

313
00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:30.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

314
00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:34.170
And I remember several people as they got up and they were talking about the different
我记得有好几个人上台发表获奖感言时，提到一个主题：编剧写了剧本，但第二讲故事的人

315
00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:40.150
awards they got, a theme was that a writer writes the script, but the second storyteller
就是剪辑师。

316
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:40.950
is the editor.
嗯哼。

317
00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:41.410
Mm-hmm.
我觉得这句话很有力量。

318
00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.170
And I thought that was really powerful.
对。

319
00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:44.270
Yeah.
没错。

320
00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:45.570
Yeah.
是啊。

321
00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:51.470
I mean, when Lee made his movie, The Giant Mechanical Man, we shot the scenes in a certain
我是说，当李拍他的电影《庞大机械人》时，我们是按照某种顺序拍摄场景的

322
00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:55.950
order, but then when he went in with his editor, they rearranged stuff.
但当他和剪辑师一起开始剪辑时，他们重新调换了顺序。

323
00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:57.610
That's crazy to me.
这对我来说太疯狂了。

324
00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:58.290
Me too.
我也是。

325
00:12:58.490 --> 00:12:58.730
Yeah.
对。

326
00:12:59.030 --> 00:12:59.410
Yeah.
没错。

327
00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:05.130
They moved certain things up or it was like, we put all the comedy in a row, maybe we want
他们把某些东西往前挪了，或者像是，我们把所有喜剧桥段都连在一起，也许我们想用一些更感伤或更触动人心的东西来打破这种节奏。

