00:27:33.890 --> 00:27:36.570
But remember, everything he's read is one-year-old.
但记住，他读到的所有内容都是一年前的。

639
00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:37.170
Right.
没错。

640
00:27:37.170 --> 00:27:40.830
Nonetheless, he orders various people into the conference room
尽管如此，他还是命令办公室里的几个人去会议室

641
00:27:40.830 --> 00:27:43.990
to brainstorm solutions to America's probleMs.
为解决美国的问题集思广益。

642
00:27:44.290 --> 00:27:45.170
I'm sorry.
不好意思。

643
00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:48.390
Is that not a conference room scene that you would love to see?
难道这不是你很想看到的会议室场景吗？

644
00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:52.630
Various members of the office brainstorming America's problems?
办公室的各个成员在为美国的各种问题集思广益？

645
00:27:52.910 --> 00:27:55.410
I mean, this is the thing that Mindy has said in interviews,
我的意思是，明蒂在采访中说过，

646
00:27:55.410 --> 00:27:59.330
that she would love to write Michael Scott's, like, take on things.
她很想写迈克尔·斯科特对事情的看法之类的东西。

647
00:27:59.530 --> 00:27:59.970
I know.
我知道。

648
00:28:00.170 --> 00:28:00.850
Like, incredible.
简直绝了。

649
00:28:01.270 --> 00:28:04.330
So, as they're doing this research,
所以，在他们做这些研究的时候，

650
00:28:05.070 --> 00:28:10.210
Dwight tells everybody that these problems are a non-issue
德怀特告诉大家这些问题根本不是问题

651
00:28:10.210 --> 00:28:13.910
because the Earth will not survive the Yellowstone supervolcano.
因为地球将无法在黄石超级火山爆发中幸存。

652
00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:18.170
Side note, that is a real thing.
顺便说一句，这是真的。

653
00:28:18.170 --> 00:28:19.030
I didn't know.
我不知道。

654
00:28:19.310 --> 00:28:19.850
What?
什么？

655
00:28:20.350 --> 00:28:22.350
The Yellowstone supervolcano.
黄石超级火山。

656
00:28:22.650 --> 00:28:23.830
I didn't know about it.
我之前不知道这事。

657
00:28:23.930 --> 00:28:24.550
Do you know about it?
你知道吗？

658
00:28:24.710 --> 00:28:25.090
No.
不知道。

659
00:28:25.510 --> 00:28:26.650
I Googled it.
我刚用谷歌查了。

660
00:28:26.810 --> 00:28:28.030
There's a supervolcano?
有个超级火山？

661
00:28:28.330 --> 00:28:33.870
There is a massive volcanic system under Yellowstone National Park.
黄石国家公园底下有一个巨大的火山系统。

662
00:28:34.330 --> 00:28:36.570
Is that why Old Faithful blows all the time?
老忠实泉一直在喷发就是因为这个吗？

663
00:28:36.730 --> 00:28:37.490
I don't know.
我不知道。

664
00:28:38.970 --> 00:28:42.410
But if it explodes, when it explodes,
但如果它爆发了，当它爆发的时候，

665
00:28:42.960 --> 00:28:46.030
they're saying it'll explode, probably not in the next hundred years,
他们说它会爆发，可能不会在接下来的一百年里，

666
00:28:46.250 --> 00:28:52.870
but eventually, it will cover most of the United States with ash and sulfur dioxide.
但最终，它会用灰烬和二氧化硫覆盖美国大部分地区。

667
00:28:53.890 --> 00:28:54.430
What?
什么？

668
00:28:54.730 --> 00:28:55.030
Yeah.
对。

669
00:28:55.210 --> 00:28:56.450
It's like an Ice Age event.
这就像是一场冰川世纪事件。

670
00:28:56.630 --> 00:28:58.290
It's just going to, like, carve everything out.
它会把一切都给铲平。

671
00:28:58.290 --> 00:28:58.750
Yes.
是的。

672
00:28:58.990 --> 00:29:03.670
To Dwight's point, nothing will matter because we're going to go into, like,
顺着德怀特的话说，一切都无所谓了，因为我们将进入，

673
00:29:03.770 --> 00:29:05.630
a decades-long volcanic winter.
长达数十年的火山冬天。

674
00:29:05.830 --> 00:29:07.070
Like, crops will die.
比如说，农作物会死光。

675
00:29:07.190 --> 00:29:08.250
Temperatures will plummet.
气温会骤降。

676
00:29:08.370 --> 00:29:09.750
It's just something to think about.
这只是个值得思考的问题。

677
00:29:09.990 --> 00:29:10.730
Worry about that.
去担心这个吧。

678
00:29:10.950 --> 00:29:11.330
Okay.
好吧。

679
00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:13.870
I need Michael Bay to get on this.
我需要迈克尔·贝来拍这个。

680
00:29:14.450 --> 00:29:17.310
He needs to cast Ben Affleck.
他得找本·阿弗莱克来主演。

681
00:29:17.550 --> 00:29:17.810
Yeah.
对。

682
00:29:18.390 --> 00:29:20.730
You know, he needs to Armageddon this shit.
你知道的，他得把这事弄得像《世界末日》一样。

683
00:29:20.990 --> 00:29:21.330
Yeah.
对。

684
00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:22.830
You know what?
你知道吗？

685
00:29:23.070 --> 00:29:24.990
It's an oppo Armageddon.
这是一场逆向的《世界末日》。

686
00:29:24.990 --> 00:29:29.890
In Armageddon, they send the oil guys, the drillers, up into space.
在《世界末日》里，他们把石油工人、钻井工送到太空去。

687
00:29:29.930 --> 00:29:30.330
I know.
我知道。

688
00:29:30.470 --> 00:29:33.750
Why don't we get a group of astronauts to dig into the volcano?
我们为什么不找一组宇航员去火山里挖洞呢？

689
00:29:33.750 --> 00:29:34.250
To go into the volcano.
深入火山里面。

690
00:29:34.750 --> 00:29:35.790
It writes itself.
这剧本简直现成。

691
00:29:35.990 --> 00:29:36.290
It does.
确实。

692
00:29:36.990 --> 00:29:38.250
Get someone on the phone.
快给谁打个电话吧。

693
00:29:38.430 --> 00:29:38.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

694
00:29:38.930 --> 00:29:40.670
Wait, do you want to watch Armageddon with me?
等等，你想和我一起看《世界末日》吗？

695
00:29:40.930 --> 00:29:42.090
When's the last time you saw it?
你上次看是什么时候？

696
00:29:42.390 --> 00:29:43.070
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

697
00:29:43.070 --> 00:29:45.090
It's been forever ago.
那是好久以前了。

698
00:29:45.690 --> 00:29:46.730
Do you want to do it?
你想看吗？

699
00:29:46.990 --> 00:29:47.650
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

700
00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:49.070
Sam, have you seen Armageddon?
萨姆，你看过《世界末日》吗？

701
00:29:49.250 --> 00:29:50.250
Yeah, I've seen Armageddon.
对，我看过《绝世天劫》。

702
00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:51.030
Like, recently?
是最近看的吗？

703
00:29:51.310 --> 00:29:51.850
No, no, no.
没有没有没有。

704
00:29:51.930 --> 00:29:52.810
Not since theaters.
自从在电影院看过之后就没看过了。

705
00:29:53.090 --> 00:29:53.610
Me either.
我也是。

706
00:29:53.610 --> 00:29:55.610
But I haven't seen it since I saw it in the theater.
不过自从在电影院看过后，我就再也没看过它。

707
00:29:56.350 --> 00:29:58.610
How is it that we all remember it so well?
为什么我们所有人都对它记得这么清楚？

708
00:29:58.770 --> 00:30:00.230
It's clearly an amazing movie.
这显然是一部了不起的电影。

709
00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:03.930
Do we need to do it as an office ladies does Armageddon?
我们需要像办公室淑女那样做一期《绝世天劫》吗？

710
00:30:04.070 --> 00:30:04.330
Yes.
要的。

711
00:30:04.450 --> 00:30:04.690
Yes.
是的。

712
00:30:04.910 --> 00:30:05.830
Some are blockbuster.
有些是大制作。

713
00:30:06.070 --> 00:30:07.830
Office ladies do Armageddon.
办公室淑女聊《绝世天劫》。

714
00:30:07.910 --> 00:30:08.550
We'll see.
我们拭目以待。

715
00:30:08.730 --> 00:30:08.970
We'll see.
走着瞧吧。

716
00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:09.470
Stay tuned.
敬请期待。

717
00:30:10.050 --> 00:30:10.370
All right.
好吧。

718
00:30:11.010 --> 00:30:12.130
Back to the plot.
回到剧情。

719
00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:14.630
Michael is going to choose a team.
迈克尔要挑选一个团队。

720
00:30:14.790 --> 00:30:20.110
He's decided that their ideas are so great, they need to get them to a representative in
他认为他们的点子太棒了，必须把它们带给一位位于

721
00:30:20.110 --> 00:30:20.990
Washington, D.C.
华盛顿特区的代表。

722
00:30:21.050 --> 00:30:21.230
Okay.
好的。

723
00:30:21.230 --> 00:30:24.730
So he chooses a team to go with him to deliver their findings.
所以他挑选了一个团队陪他去提交他们的调研结果。

724
00:30:25.050 --> 00:30:26.790
He chooses Dwight and Andy.
他选择了德怀特和安迪。

725
00:30:26.990 --> 00:30:32.030
And when they get there, and it looks like the intention was to shoot this in Washington, D.C.,
当他们到达那里时——看起来本来是打算在华盛顿特区实地拍摄的——

726
00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:33.550
they get distracted.
他们分心了。

727
00:30:33.950 --> 00:30:34.270
Oh.
哦。

728
00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:35.470
Can you believe it?
真敢相信吗？

729
00:30:35.690 --> 00:30:39.810
Michael wants to visit the Smithsonian because the set from MASH is there.
迈克尔想参观史密森尼博物馆，因为《陆军流动医院》的布景在那里。

730
00:30:40.390 --> 00:30:42.350
Dwight wants to visit the Secret Service.
德怀特想去参观特勤局。

731
00:30:42.750 --> 00:30:45.590
He also has a bone to pick with the Department of Agriculture.
他对农业部也有满腹牢骚。

732
00:30:45.590 --> 00:30:49.130
And he wants to look at the back of the Declaration of Independence.
他还想看看《独立宣言》的背面。

733
00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:57.740
According to this document, they will eventually meet their congressman.
根据这份文件，他们最终会见到他们的国会议员。

734
00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:02.700
Dwight has a complicated plan for breaking into the office and ambushing him.
德怀特有一个复杂的计划，打算潜入办公室并伏击他。

735
00:31:02.780 --> 00:31:05.900
But when they get there, it's actually not hard to get access at all.
但当他们到达那里时，其实一点也不难进去。

736
00:31:05.900 --> 00:31:10.800
The congressman is just, like, wandering around the halls, which feels to me very much like
国会议员就像是在走廊里闲逛，这让我感觉非常像

737
00:31:10.800 --> 00:31:17.180
the episode where, like, they break in to Utica and they, like, steal the whole copier.
他们潜入尤蒂卡偷走整台复印件的那集。

738
00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:17.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

739
00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:18.480
Right?
对吧？

740
00:31:18.540 --> 00:31:20.920
It's like a very elaborate plan that didn't need to be such.
就像是一个本来没必要那么复杂的精心计划。

741
00:31:21.220 --> 00:31:21.320
Exactly.
没错。

742
00:31:21.340 --> 00:31:22.420
They could just walk right in.
他们本可以直接走进去。

743
00:31:22.540 --> 00:31:22.760
Right.
对的。

744
00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:26.320
And it says, the congressman is very friendly and charming,
上面写着，国会议员非常友善迷人，

745
00:31:26.320 --> 00:31:31.740
but passes them off to an aide who gives them each a signed photo and a flag pin.
但把他们打发给了一个助手，助手给了他们每人一张亲笔签名照和一个国旗徽章。

746
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:32.400
Aw.
噢。

747
00:31:32.760 --> 00:31:33.880
That's kind of how it is.
差不多就是这样。

748
00:31:34.380 --> 00:31:36.880
They get, like, a coaster or a napkin.
他们拿到的是杯垫或者纸巾之类的东西。

749
00:31:36.940 --> 00:31:37.840
They're, like, so happy.
他们还高兴得不得了。

750
00:31:38.140 --> 00:31:38.620
Exactly.
正是如此。

751
00:31:39.060 --> 00:31:41.080
Oh, I love that so much.
哦，我太喜欢这个了。

752
00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:43.480
Gosh, the candy bags, they don't disappoint.
天哪，这些糖果袋真的没有让人失望。

753
00:31:43.620 --> 00:31:44.100
They don't.
确实没有。

754
00:31:44.260 --> 00:31:45.880
We need to do this for every character.
我们每个角色都得来这么一次。

755
00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:46.980
I agree.
我同意。

756
00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:47.460
Yeah.
是啊。

757
00:31:47.600 --> 00:31:51.460
And then we can loop back because there's more Michael Scott we didn't cover, but, you know.
然后我们可以回头再聊，因为还有很多迈克尔·斯科特的细节我们没讲到，不过嘛。

758
00:31:51.660 --> 00:31:52.040
Yeah.
是啊。

759
00:31:52.040 --> 00:31:52.500
Yeah.
对。

760
00:31:52.900 --> 00:31:54.620
Well, that's just all too much fun.
好吧，这实在太有趣了。

761
00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:57.260
And now we have an assignment, Armageddon.
现在我们有了个任务，世界末日。

762
00:31:57.400 --> 00:31:57.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

763
00:31:58.540 --> 00:32:01.560
I think we should take a break and come back with some Around the Towns.
我觉得我们应该休息一下，回来后再聊聊“周边城镇”环节。

764
00:32:01.680 --> 00:32:03.200
And our office question of the week.
还有我们每周的办公室提问环节。

765
00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:16.130
We are back, and our first Around the Town comes from Lexi T.
我们回来了，我们的第一个“周边城镇”听众来信来自爱尔兰科克郡的莱克茜·T。

766
00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.190
in County Cork, Ireland.
爱尔兰科克郡。

767
00:32:18.730 --> 00:32:20.290
Lexi wrote in and said this.
莱克茜来信说。

768
00:32:20.530 --> 00:32:27.190
This past weekend, I completed my first proper hike in preparation for the Three Peaks Challenge in the UK.
上周末，为了准备英国的“三峰挑战”，我完成了我人生中第一次真正意义上的徒步。

769
00:32:27.190 --> 00:32:38.710
The Challenge will aim to have the team summit the three highest peaks in the UK all within 24 hours in support of raising funds for cancer research in Ireland and the UK.
这项挑战旨在让团队在24小时内登顶英国三座最高峰，以此为爱尔兰和英国的癌症研究筹集资金。

770
00:32:39.050 --> 00:32:39.930
Go team!
加油，团队！

771
00:32:39.930 --> 00:32:40.850
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

772
00:32:40.990 --> 00:32:41.710
Go, Lexi.
加油，莱克茜。

773
00:32:42.250 --> 00:32:46.530
You're going to climb three mountains in 24 hours?
你打算在24小时内爬三座山？

774
00:32:46.750 --> 00:32:48.550
I don't even understand how that's possible.
我甚至无法理解这怎么可能做到。

775
00:32:48.970 --> 00:32:49.790
I don't either.
我也不理解。

776
00:32:50.030 --> 00:32:50.670
This is a feat.
这真是一项壮举。

777
00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:52.190
Lexi, I have questions.
莱克茜，我有问题想问。

778
00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:57.010
You're saying you just completed your first proper hike in preparation?
你是说你为了做准备，刚刚完成了你的第一次正式徒步？

779
00:32:57.590 --> 00:32:58.110
Wow.
哇。

780
00:32:58.330 --> 00:32:58.970
I mean, I...
我的意思是，我……

781
00:32:58.970 --> 00:33:00.850
I mean, I know people train for marathons.
我的意思是，我知道有人会为马拉松进行训练。

782
00:33:00.990 --> 00:33:01.430
That's right.
没错。

783
00:33:01.790 --> 00:33:06.910
Well, Lexi, I want to look that up because that sounds pretty impressive, and I wish you all the luck.
好吧，莱克茜，我想去查查看，因为听起来真的很厉害，祝你好运。

784
00:33:07.070 --> 00:33:09.670
I bet you're going to see some beautiful scenery as well.
我敢说你也能看到一些美丽的风景。

785
00:33:09.750 --> 00:33:10.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

786
00:33:10.550 --> 00:33:10.910
All right.
好的。

787
00:33:11.010 --> 00:33:12.770
Next up, Julia M.
接下来是来自俄亥俄州托莱多的朱莉娅·M。

788
00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:14.230
from Toledo, Ohio.
来自俄亥俄州托莱多。

789
00:33:14.570 --> 00:33:16.370
Angela, I think you're going to like this.
安吉拉，我觉得你会喜欢这个。

790
00:33:16.910 --> 00:33:24.310
Back on May 23rd this year, the Toledo Mudhens hosted a The Paper Night.
就在今年5月23日，托莱多泥母队举办了一场“纸业之夜”主题活动。

791
00:33:25.330 --> 00:33:33.450
The event featured Oscar Nunez, post-game fireworks, and a can koozie giveaway.
活动邀请了奥斯卡·努涅斯，还有赛后烟花秀以及罐套赠送。

792
00:33:34.050 --> 00:33:41.690
Um, I knew about this because, you know, I keep up with Oscar, and I saw that he was doing it, and I love the Toledo Mudhens.
嗯，我知道这个是因为，你知道的，我有关注奥斯卡，我看到他去参加了，而且我很喜欢托莱多泥母队。

793
00:33:41.710 --> 00:33:42.130
I know.
我知道。

794
00:33:42.290 --> 00:33:45.110
That's why I'm saying you've become a fan since the paper.
所以我才说自从那部剧之后你都成粉丝了。

795
00:33:45.350 --> 00:33:45.970
I've become a fan.
我确实成粉丝了。

796
00:33:46.470 --> 00:33:47.910
So, what a fun night.
真是个有趣的夜晚啊。

797
00:33:48.310 --> 00:33:48.750
All right.
好的。

798
00:33:48.810 --> 00:33:50.910
Our last around the town is from Frank B.
我们最后一个“周边城镇”来信来自明尼苏达州莱克维尔的弗兰克·B。

799
00:33:51.050 --> 00:33:52.170
in Lakeville, Minnesota.
来自明尼苏达州莱克维尔。

800
00:33:52.170 --> 00:33:53.610
Frank says,
弗兰克说：

801
00:33:54.050 --> 00:34:04.870
In Lakeville, we have our own hometown celebrity, a shirtless guy called Stickman, who spends his days walking around town carrying a giant wooden staff.
在莱克维尔，我们有自己的本地名人，一个光着膀子的家伙叫“棍夫”，他整天在镇上走来走去，手里拿着一根巨大的木棍。

802
00:34:05.090 --> 00:34:08.930
He's half Tom Hanks in Castaway and half Midwestern Gandalf.
他有一半像是《荒岛余生》里的汤姆·汉克斯，另一半像是中西部的甘道夫。

803
00:34:09.090 --> 00:34:11.910
And yes, virtually everyone knows him.
而且是的，几乎每个人都认识他。

804
00:34:12.150 --> 00:34:19.030
What started in 2007 as a local man just going out for a walk turned into one of the most wholesome traditions in town.
2007年，这只是一个当地人出门散步，后来却演变成了镇上最温馨的传统之一。

805
00:34:19.030 --> 00:34:26.050
He walks for hours every day, handing out flyers or waving at passing cards with a giant stick he found in the woods.
他每天散步数小时，用他在树林里找到的大棍子散发传单或向过往车辆挥手。

806
00:34:26.190 --> 00:34:31.050
Because apparently, Minnesotans will turn literally anything into a friendly gesture.
因为显然，明尼苏达人真的能把任何东西变成友好的手势。

807
00:34:31.470 --> 00:34:36.670
Kids get excited when they spot him, and locals proudly explain him to confuse visitors like,
孩子们看到他会很兴奋，当地人也会自豪地向困惑的游客解释说：

808
00:34:36.930 --> 00:34:38.430
Ah, that's just Stickman.
啊，那是棍夫。

809
00:34:38.430 --> 00:34:39.490
We love him.
我们爱他。

810
00:34:39.990 --> 00:34:48.130
Honestly, every community says they're unique, but not every community has a mysterious wandering folk hero who spreads joy on the local streets.
说实话，每个社区都说自己是独一无二的，但并不是每个社区都有一个神秘的流浪民间英雄，在当地的街道上传播欢乐。

811
00:34:48.130 --> 00:34:51.410
It's Lakeville does, and we're proud of our hometown hero.
莱克维尔有，我们为我们的家乡英雄感到骄傲。

812
00:34:52.110 --> 00:34:52.970
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

813
00:34:53.070 --> 00:34:54.690
